    },
    "version": 6,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "Purpose\n-------\n\nThis page documents Zimmermann's consent management approach for the new SFCC website, from a **business perspective**. It is intended to support sign-off from Zimmermann Legal on consent behaviour per storefront, and to ensure the right tracking and personalisation decisions are made before build begins.\n\nFor the technical implementation, refer to TSD: §11 Consent & Marketing.\n\n---\n\nHow consent works on the Zimmermann website\n-------------------------------------------\n\nZimmermann uses **Didomi** as its Consent Management Platform (CMP). Didomi is already live on the current Magento website and will carry over to the new SFCC site — the same licence, same configuration, same four cookie categories. The regional consent behaviour (e.g. stricter defaults for EU/UK) is already configured in Didomi and will be carried over as-is.\n\nWhen a shopper first visits the site they see a bottom-of-page banner (\"Agree and Close\" / \"Edit Preferences\" / \"Continue without agreeing\"). If they click \"Edit Preferences\", Didomi's own preference centre opens — a modal where they can toggle consent per category.\n\n**Didomi manages** (not Accenture's build scope): - The banner UI and preference centre - Storage of the shopper's consent record - Consent renewal, expiry, and regional default behaviour - Serving different consent defaults per region (carried over from current Magento configuration)\n\n**Accenture's scope** is limited to: loading the Didomi SDK in the PWA, and ensuring features we build in SFCC/PWA Kit respect the consent signal Didomi provides.\n\n---\n\nCookie categories\n-----------------\n\nZimmermann's Didomi configuration uses four categories, consistent with the published Privacy Policy:\n\n| Category | What it covers | Can shopper withdraw consent? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Required** | Strictly necessary for the site to function — login, session, basket | No — always on |\n| **Performance** | Site health monitoring, error diagnosis, server performance | Yes |\n| **Analytics** | Understanding how shoppers use the site — page views, behaviour, A/B testing, heatmapping | Yes |\n| **Marketing** | Tracking browsing behaviour to deliver personalised advertising on and off the site | Yes |\n\n---\n\nWhat should be consent-gated — full assessment\n----------------------------------------------\n\nThe table below is an independent assessment of everything on the Zimmermann website that involves tracking or personalisation. Items marked ⚠️ are gaps or uncertainties that need input.\n\n| Feature / Tool | Category | Currently on site? | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Session & basket cookies** | Required | ✅ | No consent needed. Strictly functional. |\n| **Login / authentication (SLAS)** | Required | ✅ | No consent needed. |\n| **Wishlist** | Required | ✅ | Functional feature for logged-in users. No consent needed. |\n| **Geolocation / region detection** | Required | ✅ | Used for storefront routing. Functional, no consent needed. |\n| **reCAPTCHA** | Required (except EU/UK) | ✅ | Security tool, not tracking. No consent needed except in EU/UK where it is consent-gated per current Didomi configuration. |\n| **Booxi** (boutique appointment booking) | Required | ✅ | Functional booking tool. |\n| **Google Analytics / GA4** | Analytics | ✅ | Via GTM / Tell No Lies. |\n| **Crazy Egg** (heatmapping & session replay) | Analytics | ✅ | Records mouse movements, clicks, scrolls. Loaded directly by PWA, post-consent. |\n| **Optimizely** (A/B testing) | Analytics | ✅ | US storefront only. Loaded directly by PWA, post-consent. |\n| **Recently Viewed products** | Required? | ✅ | ⚠️ Currently tracks even when consent is dismissed or rejected on AU/EU — confirm intended behaviour |\n| **Einstein Recommendations** (\"You May Also Like\") | Analytics | ✅ | Personalisation based on browsing behaviour. Consent needed. |\n| **Narvar EDD widget** (delivery estimates at checkout) | Performance | ✅ (domestic) | ⚠️ Category not yet confirmed — Performance or Analytics? Needs input from Zimmermann / Narvar. |\n| **Vimeo** (product videos) | ⚠️ TBC | ✅ | Vimeo can track viewing behaviour. Option: use `dnt=1` embed parameter when consent not granted, or gate fully behind a category. Confirm approach with Zimmermann. |\n| **Measmerize** | Marketing | ✅ | Named in Zimmermann's privacy policy under Marketing & Advertising. Loaded by PWA — we need to confirm the exact Didomi category so we gate it correctly. Owner: Tell No Lies / Zimmermann. |\n| **Facebook Pixel** | Marketing | ✅ | Named in privacy policy. Via GTM / Tell No Lies. |\n| **Pinterest** | Marketing | ✅ | Via GTM / Tell No Lies. |\n| **TikTok Pixel** | Marketing | ✅ | Via GTM / Tell No Lies. |\n| **Google Ads / conversion tracking** | Marketing | ✅ | Via GTM / Tell No Lies. |\n| **Inside Chat** | GTM-managed | ✅ | Fully managed by Tell No Lies inside the GTM container. Consent gating is Tell No Lies' responsibility — not in Accenture's scope. |\n| **Marketing email opt-in** | Not cookie-based | ✅ | This is a separate consent from cookie consent — marketing communications opt-in, managed via Omneo → Emarsys. Not in scope here. |\n| **Size / fit preferences** | ⚠️ TBC | ⚠️ | If size or fit preferences are remembered across sessions via a cookie, category needs to be confirmed. |\n\n---\n\nOpen items\n----------\n\n| # | Question | Owner |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | Confirm intended behaviour for **Recently Viewed** when consent is not granted — should tracking be suppressed? Current Magento AU site tracks regardless of consent. | Zimmermann Legal |\n| 2 | Confirm **Measmerize** Didomi purpose / category so the PWA can gate it correctly. | Tell No Lies / Zimmermann |\n| 3 | Confirm **Narvar EDD widget** Didomi category — Performance or Analytics? | Zimmermann / Narvar |\n| 4 | Confirm **Vimeo** consent approach — gate fully behind a category, or use `dnt=1` embed parameter when consent not granted? | Zimmermann |\n| 5 | Confirm whether **size / fit preferences** are persisted via cookie and if so, what category applies. | Zimmermann |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f36a",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

